\title{MEWOC: Modified Escalation with Overdose Control for Single-Agent Phase I Trials}
\description{
Bayesian dose finding for single-agent phase I trials with escalation with
overdose control (EWOC), using the reparameterized model in which clinicians
give prior probabilities that the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) lies below the
minimum or above the maximum trial dose. Doses may be discrete levels or a
continuous range.
}
\details{
Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=run_mewoc_grid_search]{run_mewoc_grid_search()}} calibrates the prior hyperparameters (BOBYQA).
\item \code{\link[=build_prior_plot]{build_prior_plot()}} displays the prior probability of a dose-limiting
toxicity (DLT) at each dose.
\item \code{\link[=run_single_trial_simulation]{run_single_trial_simulation()}} and \code{\link[=run_trial_simulations_background]{run_trial_simulations_background()}}
simulate trials; \code{\link[=summarize_trial_simulation_results]{summarize_trial_simulation_results()}} gives the operating
characteristics.
\item \code{\link[=build_conduct_design_table]{build_conduct_design_table()}}, \code{\link[=conduct_trial_rule_rows]{conduct_trial_rule_rows()}},
\code{\link[=build_conduct_patient_template]{build_conduct_patient_template()}} and \code{\link[=write_conduct_workbook]{write_conduct_workbook()}} create the
Trial Conduct workbook; \code{\link[=conduct_evaluate_trial]{conduct_evaluate_trial()}} evaluates trial data
cohort by cohort and recommends the dose for the next cohort.
\item \code{\link[=run_mewoc_app]{run_mewoc_app()}} starts the interactive 'shiny' application.
}

Posterior computation uses 'JAGS' through the 'rjags' package; JAGS must be
installed (\url{https://mcmc-jags.sourceforge.io/}).
}
